+// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+// Xbox360PS5, fix 150d: a device whose files live in memory, for the guest's utility cache.
+// Grand Theft Auto IV copies its streaming archives (.img) from the disc into cache: and cache1:
+// every session: about 1.98 GiB in all within 5 min in memory (1.0.6-work-fix150d), while on a
+// drive past its write burst the copy never finished (1.41 GiB in a 6 min session, the old
+// session's files deleted first). The console gives the emulator's process one burst of about 1.5 GB of drive
+// writes per start (bench 148i: then about 2 MiB/s, on /data and the M.2 alike), and from about
+// 3 min into GTA IV every file operation waited on a ~0.95 s tick (1.0.6-work-fix146f-150-152-153).
+// In memory the cache writes and frees nothing on a drive. Nothing needs to outlive the process:
+// the game copies the files again when they are missing (it did so every session anyway).
+//
+// The bytes come from file mappings (xe::memory::CreateFileMappingHandle, as the guest's own
+// memory: direct memory on the console, not the small flexible heap of malloc), in segments of
+// kSegmentBytes cut into kChunkBytes chunks. A file holds its chunks sparsely (a hole reads as
+// zeros); a delete, a shorter length or the end of the entry gives them back at once, and a segment
+// none of whose chunks is used is unmapped. At most Pool::cap bytes are in use, and no segment is
+// mapped while the console's direct memory would fall below Pool::reserve; a write that would
+// need more fails with STATUS_DISK_FULL (the game then streams that file from the disc). The use,
+// the peak, the refusals, the files (deleted ones still open counted apart), the bytes given back
+// and the largest files are added to fix 148d's 30 s File I/O line.
+//
+// The entries keep fixes 129, 139 and 139b's rules (entry.cc): a deleted file's entry leaves its
+// directory at once and keeps its data for the handles still open on it (as an unlinked host
+// file), freed with the entry when the last one closes.
+#ifndef XENIA_VFS_DEVICES_MEMORY_DEVICE_H_
+#define XENIA_VFS_DEVICES_MEMORY_DEVICE_H_
+
